      "evidenceText": "Truth & Beauty / Moritz Stefaner — independent data visualization expert Skip to content Truth & Beauty — Moritz Stefaner, independent data visualization designer and consultant What I do Hi. My name is Moritz Stefaner. I live and breathe data visualization — as an independent designer and consultant. I help organizations, researchers and businesses to find truth and beauty in relevant and meaningful data. How could we work together? Let me know! Featured projects A Hidden Infrastructure Mapping the underground world of fungi Climate—Conflict—Vulnerability Index Mapping the overlap between climate and conflict risks WHO Data Design Language Rich data experiences for public health data Impfdashboard The official German COVID-19 vaccination dashboard Peak Spotting Managing passenger loads in the German rail network OECD Better Life Index How's life? more projects Fresh Nov ’26 BikeNetKit Can open-source data tools accelerate the green transition of European cities? BikeNetKit presents a suite of tools to grow, link and fix bicycle networks, based on cutting-edge research algorithms. The website features five interactive maps with precomputed results for 412 European cities, made for planners, cycling advocates and anyone who wants to argue for a better bike network in their town. Oct ’26 Beyond the bar chart My talk at KIKK Festival 2026 in the Grande Salle of the Théâtre de Namur: Do we still need expert-designed visualizations in an age of automated chart generation? Sep ’26 Underground Science. Underground Stories. At the Narrative Change Summit of the Climate Film Festival during NYC Climate Week, I joined a session convened by SPUN on why data alone so rarely moves people, and what makes science stick. I showed how we turned SPUN's maps of underground fungal networks into A Hidden Infrastructure , then talked science storytelling with Toby Kiers (SPUN), Alessandra Yupanqui (Sapiens) and Willow Defebaugh (Atmos), moderated by Mandy Nguyen. more appearances",
