sets effectively. Docs highlights Dive deeper into dbt Learn best practices, explore detailed configuration references, or review our APIs. Documentation API Docs Product Docs Best Practices dbt Wizard Guides Quickstart for dbt and Snowflake Quickstart for dbt and Databricks Airflow and dbt Debugging errors Reference Guides Command Reference Project Configurations dbt Artifacts Other Resources Release Notes Developer Blog Join the Community Get help from others Join the dbt Community Connect with thousands of developers solving real data problems every day. Join Slack Ask questions, get answers, and meet people who speak your data language. GitHub Discussions Join technical threads or open issues. Subscribe to the newsletter Get fresh community ideas, job posts, and tools delivered weekly. Answer a question on Discourse Help someone solve a real problem—and build your reputation doing it. Webinars Upcoming and on-demand sessions from dbt Labs. Events Meetups, conferences, and community gatherings. Courses & Tutorials Learn dbt with hands-on guidance. From the team Read the developer blog Deep dives, changelogs, best practices, and new feature highlights from dbt Labs. A checklist for getting the most out of dbt State A step-by-step checklist for teams adopting dbt State on a large dbt project, from baselining performance to consolidating jobs. analytics craft Read more Have dbt skills been bitter lesson’d? Models have improved a lot since we shipped dbt agent skills, so I ran Claude Opus, Sonnet, and Haiku 5.5, and then Sonnet 4.5, through a... ai Read more Inside the dbt Wizard harness: building an agent that thinks in DAGs Wizard works like an analytics engineer: it thinks in DAGs, tests and fixes its own work, and keeps you in flow, so you review a working... ai Read more",
